    "description": "ACES Delta is a large-scale clean hydrogen production and storage project in Delta, Utah. Its target end markets include long-duration power storage and industrial decarbonization applications that require dispatchable low-carbon hydrogen. The project is asset-heavy and development-oriented, with economics tied to electrolysis, salt-cavern storage, and long-duration energy infrastructure rather than to a conventional merchant generation asset. U.S. Department of Energy materials state that the facility combines 220 MW of alkaline electrolysis with two 4.5 million barrel salt caverns capable of supporting long-duration storage. The reviewed materials did not disclose project-level revenue or GIC's ownership percentage within the broader equity syndication consortium. Public materials show that DOE closed a US$504.4 million loan guarantee in 2022 and that GIC participated through a Haddington-led equity financing program around the project.",
